# Falcon 2.0

Falcon 2.0 is the design system for Web, Android, and iOS. One system, three implementations.

## Platforms

- Specify every component, token, and pattern for Web, Android, and iOS.
- A component is incomplete until all three platforms are specified, or a written exception names the platforms it skips and why.
- Keep meaning, hierarchy, and tokens the same. Adapt interaction to the platform: keyboard and hover on web, touch and system gestures on mobile.

## Tokens

Color, typography, spacing, radius, elevation, and motion come from `styles/foundations.css`. Reference those variables by name.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
button { background: #009A78; padding: 0 20px; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
button { background: var(--gradient-primary); padding: 0 var(--pad-button-x); }
```

## Naming

Use the same component and token names on every platform: `Button`, `brand/500`, `space/4`. Map those names into platform syntax. Do not invent a second palette.

## Accessibility

- Text contrast meets WCAG AA.
- Interactive targets are at least 44×44 px on web, 48×48 dp on Android, and 44×44 pt on iOS.
- Every control has an accessible name. Web shows a visible focus ring. Android uses `contentDescription`. iOS uses VoiceOver labels.
